    "categoryId": "java",
    "companyId": null,
    "part": 1,
    "prompt": "Checked vs unchecked exceptions — and what do you use in production?",
    "answerHtml": "<p>Checked (<code>IOException</code>, <code>SQLException</code>) — compiler-enforced, recoverable. Unchecked (<code>RuntimeException</code> family) — programming errors. Errors (<code>OutOfMemoryError</code>, <code>StackOverflowError</code>) — don't catch.\nIn modern Spring services, most teams prefer <strong>unchecked</strong> custom exceptions (<code>ResourceNotFoundException extends RuntimeException</code>) plus a <code>@RestControllerAdvice</code> handler, because checked exceptions pollute signatures and don't compose with lambdas/streams.</p>",
    "followUps": [],
    "tags": [],
    "source": "interview-prep.html"
