    "prompt": "How is logging done centrally?",
    "answerHtml": "<p class=\"tldr\"><strong>In one line</strong> — structured JSON to stdout with a correlation ID, shipped by an agent, indexed in Elasticsearch, queried in Kibana.</p><ol>\n<li>Service logs JSON with a correlation ID from MDC</li>\n<li>Shipper (Filebeat/Fluent Bit, a DaemonSet on K8s) tails the log stream, tracks its offset so it resumes after restart, batches and forwards</li>\n<li>Logstash optionally parses, enriches, masks sensitive fields</li>\n<li>Elasticsearch indexes into time-based indices with an ILM policy that rolls over and expires them</li>\n<li>Kibana queries</li>\n</ol><p class=\"bonus\"><strong>Say this too</strong> — the <strong>correlation ID</strong> is what makes it useful — it's what lets you reconstruct one user journey across services. Logs answer \"what happened\"; traces answer \"where did the time go\".</p>",
    "followUps": [],
