    "prompt": "How does DNS work?",
    "answerHtml": "<p class=\"tldr\"><strong>In one line</strong> — the resolver checks caches, then a recursive resolver walks root → TLD → authoritative, caching the answer for its TTL.</p><ul>\n<li>Records: A/AAAA addresses · CNAME alias · MX mail · TXT verification · NS delegation · SRV service location.</li>\n<li>Why it matters here: it's how Kubernetes service discovery works, and TTLs govern how fast a failover actually takes effect.</li>\n</ul><p class=\"gotcha\"><strong>Gotcha</strong> — the <strong>JVM has its own DNS cache</strong> — <code>networkaddress.cache.ttl</code>. Historically it kept services hammering a dead IP long after a failover. Set it explicitly.</p>",
