    "topicId": "company--10-design-patterns-solid",
    "categoryId": "company",
    "companyId": "epam",
    "part": 10,
    "prompt": "Explain the Strategy pattern with an example.",
    "answerHtml": "<p class=\"tldr\"><strong>In one line</strong> — encapsulate interchangeable algorithms behind one interface so the caller stops branching.</p><ul>\n<li><code>PaymentProcessor</code> with card, PayPal and crypto implementations.</li>\n<li>Spring injects them all as a <code>List</code> or a <code>Map</code> keyed by type; the service looks up the right one.</li>\n</ul><p class=\"bonus\"><strong>Say this too</strong> — this <em>is</em> the Open/Closed Principle in practice — a new payment type is a new class and zero edits to existing code.</p>",
